<title>UK: WH Smith down as chief executive quits.</title>
<headline>WH Smith down as chief executive quits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in WH Smith Group Plc dropped in pre-market trade on Monday after the retail group said its chief executive Bill Cockburn would leave in October to join British Telecommunications Plc.</p>
<p>WH Smith shares were down 20-1/2p at 391 by 0722 GMT in volume of 35,000 shares.</p>
<p>Smith said Cockburn will join BT as group managing director, adding that results for the year ended May 31 would be in line with market expectations.</p>
</text>
